    "summary": "Read the control receipt (26c0509e6788479a87a674b2d686b134, completed, tests_passed, exit 0, no changed target files) and recorded the final revision. Both control comparisons hold with complete admissions: index 7 is the CheckQuorum setup (true, election timeout 3, StateLeader, three voters), index 8 shows 24 retries across three ticks ending at StateFollower with window_closed=true, and index 9 shows eight further reads after the step-down left the queue at 24 unchanged (pending_unchanged=true, unconfirmed 0). The same receipt also carries the growth, admitted and drain cases (indices 1-6), so one receipt now covers the whole predicate and all declared comparisons across the investigation evaluated holds. I promoted the control to a durable fact tied to indices 8 and 9 and revised the interpretation to cite indices 1,2,4,6,8,9, refining applicability rather than substance: the competing 'transient state' explanation is partly right (CheckQuorum does close the window within an election timeout) but refuted for retention (the queue survived the step-down and further reads) and for the library default (CheckQuorum false, where nothing closes it). The defect claim stays asserted - no library-side bound on retained caller state, no reclamation, one heartbeat per retry plus a release burst - with the refusal to answer reads without quorum explicitly not the complaint, and severity still unassessed alongside the modelled-trigger, single-depth and fixed-retry-rate limitations."
